if you thought Justice League was a mess  it's important to remember things could  have been far far worse back in 1997  Joel Schumacher's Batman and Robin and  nearly ruined comic book movies forever  but surprisingly enough it wasn't the  worst comic adaptation of that year  CBS took a shot on piloting a TV series  called Justice League of America but the  results made Batman and Robin that look  like The Dark Knight the premise was  simple in fact a little too simple it's  entered a Matthew settle as Green  Lantern alongside Kenny Johnston's the  flash john kassir as the atom and  michelle herd as fire these are all  characters that have been associated  with Justice League in the comics but  the kicker in this adaptation is that  they were all roommates and regular  people with ordinary problems  it's as if CBS asked for DC's  Superfriends meets NBC's friends what is  the matter with you in fact it'd be  shocking if that exact phrase didn't  come up during a pitch meeting Justice  League of America turns out to be a  weird amalgam of an action drama and a  sitcom except the special effects were  embarrassing even by 90 standards and  the comedy was downright painful that  were also extremely awkward interview  segments of the characters scattered  throughout giving the whole thing a  quasi mockumentary feel that interrupted  any semblance of flow it might have had  but a lot of the problems came from the  would be series botting the iconic  characters up there cause Green Lantern  was shown as a software salesman and was  based on guy gardner from the comics  while looking more at the kyle rayner  version and being as Dulles Hal Jordan  from the Superfriends cartoon if it's a  just you wanted to trust you'll get  meanwhile the flash was depicted as  struggling with unemployment despite a  SuperSpeed the Assam was a science  teacher who could shrink himself small  enough to fix an old school TV and fire  was a struggling actress who definitely  dressed up as a banana for a commercial  audition then there was Martian  Manhunter played by David Ogden Stiers  from mash whose face was always covered  with a budget version of what Jim Carrey  wore in the mask well though that might  all sound a little like some hokey  remake of The Incredibles  it wasn't it wasn't good enough each  character was unlikable in his or her  own way and the plot was even worse in  the episode the team recruits a new  member in ice who started out as a  meteorologist in the town of new Metro  yes that was the actual completely  uninspired name of a city from the show  after a freak lab accident gave White's  the ability to freeze things she worked  with the other heroes to take down the  villainous weatherman played by the late  great and Miguel Ferrer since the show  didn't get past the pilot it's not clear  if the plan was to feature a new villain  in each episode but for red there's a  serviceable job in one of his trademark  bad guy roles but even that wasn't  enough to redeem it the biggest problem  of Justice League of America was that it  couldn't figure out if it was a sitcom  or something more serious  while modern shows like arrow Supergirl  and Marvel's agents of shield find  subtle ways to use humour as a balance  for the darker moments this show went  way too far into family-friendly cheese  to ever make anything seem consequential  Justice League of America never hit the  air in the US although some overseas  markets may have seen it however the  pilot still has life thanks to the  wonders of the internet and the bootleg  screening shown at comic book  conventions but it's not a cult  following that's developed in the wake  of its modern availability it mostly  just serves as a cautionary tale about  half-heartedly adapting beloved comic  book characters when you have little to  no budget or creative vision  some people run away we were all into  different stuff two decades ago but it's  difficult to believe  anyone would have ever been into this  although Zack Snyder's Justice League  didn't do as well as expected at the  box-office and critics were certainly  not kind it looks like a legitimate  masterpiece compared to this show  Bastogne thanks for watching click the  loop icon to subscribe to our YouTube  channel plus check out all this cool  stuff we know your love to  [Music]
 

